WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Experience should travel.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Two levels. One memory.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Start with simulation knowledge. Act in the physical world.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Record what the robot did — and what physically happened.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
The trajectory becomes evidence for knowledge maintenance.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Cover + press simulation priors are maintained with Task 1 experience.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.500
A different task. The same growing knowledge system.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Complete the count before switching targets.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Task Knowledge guides the sequence. Action Knowledge supports contact.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Maintain the store again, using this new physical experience.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:58.000
The maintained store now becomes the input to a composed task.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Now combine the skills: uncover, count, and press.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Retrieve placement knowledge that already applies to this scene.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.000
The revealed blocks require red ×2, green ×1, and blue ×1.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:21.000
Task 3 retrieves a strategy maintained from Task 2.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:27.000
Different scene. Reusable strategy. Grounded in the current goal.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:33.000
The second retrieved strategy completes the two-press sequence.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.000
Reuse the knowledge. Re-ground the geometry.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:41.000
An uncertain blue-button effect stays uncertain in the automatic record.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Turn physical experience into reusable knowledge.

